            "presentation_state": "show_all",
            "properties": {
                "0": {
                    "name": "block",
                    "value": "Makes an array of random whole numbers from low up to, but not including, high - each one equally likely. low 1 and high 7 rolls dice.\n\nUse it to pick random indices (which joint, which sample, which preset), random steps of a scale, random MIDI notes in a range, random delays in whole frames.\n\nSYNTAX:\nnp.random.integers <dims ...>\nDefault: 10 values.\n\nEXAMPLE:\nnp.random.integers 5\n\nINPUTS and PARAMETERS:\n\n(button):\nMakes a new array and sends it.\n\nshape (text box, also an inlet):\nThe size along each axis.\n\nlow (int box, also an inlet):\nThe smallest possible value.\n\nhigh (int box, also an inlet):\nOne more than the largest possible value: high itself never comes up. It must be above low.\n\nseed:\nAn option, under the node. -1 (the default) draws different numbers every time the patch opens. Any other number starts the same sequence every time - the same \"random\" piece on every run, which is what you want for rehearsal, comparison and debugging.\n\nOUTPUTS:\n\nrandom array:\nThe whole numbers (64-bit integers).\n\nREADING THE DEMO:\nFive dice, low 1 and high 7, rolled twice a second. Each is 1 to 6, never 7.\n\nRELATED:\nnp.random.choice picks from any list, with weights. np.rand and np.random.normal give decimals. random gives a single random number.",
                    "value_type": "str"
                },
                "1": {
                    "name": "lock",
                    "value": true,
                    "value_type": "bool"
                },
                "2": {
                    "name": "width",
                    "value": 760,
                    "value_type": "int"
                },
                "3": {
                    "name": "height",
                    "value": 900,
                    "value_type": "int"
                },
                "4": {
                    "name": "text_size",
                    "value": "30",
                    "value_type": "str"
                }
            },
            "text": "Makes an array of random whole numbers from low up to, but not including, high - each one equally likely. low 1 and high 7 rolls dice.\n\nUse it to pick random indices (which joint, which sample, which preset), random steps of a scale, random MIDI notes in a range, random delays in whole frames.\n\nSYNTAX:\nnp.random.integers <dims ...>\nDefault: 10 values.\n\nEXAMPLE:\nnp.random.integers 5\n\nINPUTS and PARAMETERS:\n\n(button):\nMakes a new array and sends it.\n\nshape (text box, also an inlet):\nThe size along each axis.\n\nlow (int box, also an inlet):\nThe smallest possible value.\n\nhigh (int box, also an inlet):\nOne more than the largest possible value: high itself never comes up. It must be above low.\n\nseed:\nAn option, under the node. -1 (the default) draws different numbers every time the patch opens. Any other number starts the same sequence every time - the same \"random\" piece on every run, which is what you want for rehearsal, comparison and debugging.\n\nOUTPUTS:\n\nrandom array:\nThe whole numbers (64-bit integers).\n\nREADING THE DEMO:\nFive dice, low 1 and high 7, rolled twice a second. Each is 1 to 6, never 7.\n\nRELATED:\nnp.random.choice picks from any list, with weights. np.rand and np.random.normal give decimals. random gives a single random number."
        },
